# Line-ending policy.
#
# Why this file exists: the GitHub windows-latest image ships core.autocrlf=true,
# so a plain checkout hands the tests CRLF text while the generators emit LF.
# src-tauri/src/model/matrix.rs (read_repo_file + between_markers) compares those
# bytes literally, so two doc-freshness tests failed on Windows only:
#   model::matrix::tests::detection_doc_matrix_matches_the_code
#   model::matrix::tests::evidence_index_documents_every_proven_route
# Forcing LF in the working tree on every OS makes the checkouts deterministic.
# Generated-doc scripts also hash the files (policy-check job), so the on-disk
# bytes must not depend on the runner's OS.

# Text we compare or hash byte-for-byte in tests, scripts and CI.
*.rs     text eol=lf
*.toml   text eol=lf
*.lock   text eol=lf
*.md     text eol=lf
*.sh     text eol=lf
*.py     text eol=lf
*.js     text eol=lf
*.mjs    text eol=lf
*.json   text eol=lf
*.yml    text eol=lf
*.yaml   text eol=lf
*.html   text eol=lf
*.css    text eol=lf
*.txt    text eol=lf
*.csv    text eol=lf
*.tsv    text eol=lf
*.ps1    text eol=lf
*.cfb    text eol=lf

# Fixtures and captured artifacts are binary inputs to the conversion matrix.
# Git must never rewrite a byte of them, on any platform.
fixtures/**          binary
spikes/*/artifacts/** binary
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.webp binary
*.avif binary
*.ico  binary
*.heic binary
*.tif  binary
*.bmp  binary
